{
  "opening": "The boltons library is releasing version 19.1.0, which introduces several enhancements to its utility modules. The glom project depends on boltons and must update to this release to ensure compatibility with the new public API behaviors.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m08",
      "text": "In the boltons library, the OneToOne class must handle non-unique one-to-one inputs without raising errors, maintaining the integrity of the FastIterOrderedMultiDict structure. The unique function should correctly process inputs where keys are not strictly unique, returning appropriate results."
    },
    {
      "id": "m12",
      "text": "In the boltons library, the FunctionBuilder class's get_arg_names method must return argument names including keyword-only arguments. Its get_defaults_dict method must include defaults for keyword-only arguments, ensuring consistency with Python 3+ annotations via formatargandannotation."
    },
    {
      "id": "m12c",
      "text": "When observed through glom's tests, the boltons library's FunctionBuilder class must expose get_arg_names and get_defaults_dict methods that correctly handle keyword-only argument defaults. The inspect_formatargspec and formatargandannotation utilities must function without Python 3 warnings, supporting get_module_callables."
    },
    {
      "id": "m19",
      "text": "In the boltons library, the difference_update method must support the __rsub__ operator for complement-set operations. This ensures that set difference updates behave correctly when used in reverse subtraction contexts."
    },
    {
      "id": "m22",
      "text": "In the glom project, the Glommer class and related spec types like Auto, Check, Fill, First, Iter, Let, Spec, and TType must remain functional after merging master into partial. Core functions such as all, chunked, dropwhile, fill, filter, first, flatten, glom, and glomit must continue to process data transformations without errors."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please verify these changes in both projects to ensure seamless integration. The consumer project should run its test suite against the updated host release."
}
